Scenario ID: S06
Scenario title: Vendor Meeting and Improvement Action Follow-up
Initial workflow description:
The team meets with an equipment vendor to discuss improvement ideas. After the meeting, someone summarizes the discussion and follows up on action items.

Domain expert answers:
{
  "answers": [
    {
      "question_id": "Q1",
      "question": "What event or condition triggers the scheduling of a vendor meeting — is it recurring on a fixed schedule, initiated by a specific operational issue, or requested on an ad hoc basis?",
      "answer": "The meeting is triggered by an improvement request or an equipment issue summary. It is not described as recurring on a fixed schedule; rather, it is initiated when a specific operational need or improvement idea arises. The equipment engineer prepares the agenda and issue summary first, which then prompts the meeting organizer to schedule the vendor meeting."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q2",
      "question": "Which roles or departments are typically involved in the vendor meeting, and who holds primary responsibility for organizing it and producing the post-meeting summary?",
      "answer": "Roles involved include the equipment engineer, vendor representative, meeting organizer, action-item owner, and manager. The meeting organizer holds primary responsibility for scheduling the meeting and producing the post-meeting summary. The equipment engineer leads the technical discussion with the vendor."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q3",
      "question": "In what format is the meeting discussion currently captured — for example, a free-text email, a structured template, or recorded notes — and is there a standard tool or system used to store this output?",
      "answer": "Decisions and open questions are recorded during the meeting by the meeting organizer. The output is stored as meeting notes and shared via a shared document repository. The specific format (e.g., free-text vs. structured template) is not specified in the workflow."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q4",
      "question": "When action items are identified from the meeting, how are they recorded and assigned — do they include a designated owner, a due date, and a priority level, and if so, where is this information stored?",
      "answer": "Action items are assigned owners and due dates by the manager after the meeting. They are stored in an action-item tracker. Priority level is not explicitly mentioned in the workflow. The action-item list with owner and due date assignments is also included in the shared meeting summary."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q5",
      "question": "How is follow-up on action items currently conducted — for example, through manual email reminders, a task management system, or periodic review meetings — and how frequently does this occur?",
      "answer": "Action-item progress is tracked by the action-item owner using an action-item tracker. The workflow identifies automated reminders and status tracking as an automation opportunity, implying follow-up is currently more manual. The specific frequency of follow-up reviews is not specified."
    },
    {
      "question_id": "Q6",
      "question": "What criteria must be met for this workflow to be considered fully complete — is it when all action items are marked closed, when a final summary report is approved, or some other condition?",
      "answer": "The workflow does not explicitly define a formal completion criterion. Based on the workflow structure, the process concludes when action-item progress is tracked by owners following distribution of the meeting summary. A specific condition such as all items closed or a final report approved is not specified."
    }
  ]
}
